Description: Honor CPPFLAGS and LDFLAGS in every link rule
 Debian's build flags (hardening, -Wl,--as-needed, etc.) are passed via
 the CPPFLAGS and LDFLAGS environment variables, but the upstream
 makefile never referenced either in most of its link rules, so those
 flags were silently dropped. This adds $(LDFLAGS) to every link
 command.
 .
 Several targets (add_off, chinese, colors, colors2, desigcgi, dist,
 easter, gtest, htc20b, marstime, mpc2sof, mpc_code, mpc_time,
 parallax, parallax.cgi, ps_1996, relativi, sof, solseqn, spline,
 them_cat, and cgicheck) compile their .cpp/.c source directly in the
 same command as the link step, instead of going through the general
 .cpp.o/.c.o rules that already carry $(CPPFLAGS). Since
 -I/usr/include/pluto (where libpluto-jpl-eph-dev installs its
 headers) only comes from $(CPPFLAGS), any of these targets that need
 a header from there fail once make actually reaches them, e.g.:
 .
   mpc2sof.cpp:22:10: fatal error: watdefs.h: No such file or directory
 .
 This was only noticed one target at a time, as progressively fixing
 earlier build blockers let make reach further into this list, so
 fix $(CPPFLAGS) on all of them at once rather than one at a time.
Author: Fukui Daichi <a.dog.will.talk@akane.waseda.jp>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-08
